{"type":"thinking","text":"Now I can decode the HUD nametable (nametable 0, rows 3,5,6, x=10..21):\n\nRow 3 (y=24-31): \nx=11: 247 (0xF7) = rupee icon? palette1\nx=12: 33 (0x21) = \"X\" (the letter X)\nx=13: 0 = \"0\" digit? Wait tile 0 might be the digit \"0\". Hmm x=13 tile 0.\nx=14: 36 (blank)\nx=15: 105 (0x69), x=16: 11, x=17: 107, x=18: 105, x=19: 10, x=20: 107\nThese tiles 105,11,107,105,10,107 = \"B\" ... hmm. Actually row3 x=15-20 is the \"B\" box border? tiles 0x69,0x0B,0x6B,0x69,0x0A,0x6B. That's the B box top. Wait, the B box is at x~150-165 → tiles 18-20. Hmm 15-20 = x=120-167. The B box left edge at x=15? The screenshot shows B box around x=148-168 (tiles 18-20) and A box x=180-200 (tiles 22-25).\n\nHmm wait, row3 x=22-28: 36,98,21,18,15,14,98 → that's \"LIFE\"? tiles 98,21,18,15,14,98 = maybe \"-LIFE-\". Actually at x=23:98, x=24:21, x=25:18, x=26:15, x=27:14, x=28:98. Hmm the LIFE text. And x=22 blank, x=29 blank.\n\nWait, that doesn't match; the LIFE text in screenshot is at x~185-230 → tiles 23-28. Yes! So tiles 98='-', 21='L', 18='I', 15='F', 14='E', 98='-'. Great, so this row3 is the top row of HUD text: rupee icon + X0 at x=11-13, B box at 15-20?, LIFE at 23-28.\n\nHmm, but the B box and A box: The B box is drawn at x=15-17? and A at ... Actually row 4: x=15:108, x=17:108, x=18:108, x=20:108 = box verticals. So B box spans x=15..17? no.\n\nLet me re-map using screen coords: tile x * 8.\n- x=11 → 88-95: rupee icon (tile F7)\n- x=12 → 96-103: \"X\" (tile 21 = 'X')\n- x=13 → 104-111: digit (tile 0 = '0')\n- x=14 → 112-119: blank\n- B box: x=15..17? verticals at x=15 and x=17 → box 24px wide? 120-143. Hmm but screenshot B box around x=120-144. Yes! B box is x=15-17, with letter B at top? Actually top row x=15:105,16:11,17:107 = box top with 'B' at 16 (tile 11='B'?). \n- x=18: blank, x=19..20: A box? row3 x=19:105? no row3 x=19=105, x=20=107. Hmm.\n\nWait row3: x=15:105, x=16:11, x=17:107, x=18:105, x=19:10, x=20:107. So there are two boxes: B box x=1