tine, which also writes the heart tiles. Then I can cross-reference the PC.\n\nActually, the trace write on heart tiles gave PC 0xA0D6. Let me trace reads on RAM 0x0000-0x07FF for 2 frames and find reads whose pc = 0xA0D6 (or nearby). Those reads would be the health source!\n\nLet me do: trace_writes mode read, address 0, length 2048, frames 2. Hmm, length max 256! \"length: Bytes in the range (default 1, max 256)\". So I'd need multiple traces. \n\nAlternatively I can trace reads on candidate ranges. The health is likely in 0x0600-0x06FF. Let me trace reads on 0x0600 length 256, frames 4, mode read. Then look for reads with PC 0xA0D6 or similar. But the trace may return aggregated per (pc, address). Let me see.\n\nBut wait — the game must run frames. It's paused; trace will run frames (refused while paused?). It said refused while paused. Let me resume, then trace. But the game runs and Link might move; that's fine for 4 frames.\n\nLet me first load clean again to have 3 hearts (I've written 0x000D=1). Actually it doesn't matter much.\n\nHmm, this is getting long. Let me think about a smarter ground-truth method.\n\n**Key insight**: The HUD redraws the heart tiles every 2 frames from the health variable. If I can trace the READS that happen at the same PC that writes the heart tiles, I get the health variable directly.\n\nThe write PC is 0xA0D6. Let me trace reads of RAM 0x0600-0x06FF for 4 frames and see if any read has pc near 0xA0D6.\n\nLet me do it. First resume? trace runs frames. Let me just call trace_writes mode read.\n\nActually, maybe trace_writes while paused is refused, but maybe it auto-resumes. The description says refused while paused. Let me resume first.\n\nBut careful: the game running from clean will stay on the start screen (no input) and Link won't move. Good.\n\nLet me resume then trace reads on 0x0600 len 256 frames 4.\n\nHmm, but 4 frames might catch the HUD routine (every 2 frames). Let me do frames=6.\n\nLet me resume and trace."}
