eleport Link.\n\nAlternatively, note the health is probably NOT in OAM 0x02xx. Let me exclude 0x0200-0x02FF (OAM) and 0x0300 (tile buffer) and test the rest: candidates in wd1 outside 0x0200-0x02FF: \n0x0004, 0x0005, 0x000A, 0x000F, 0x0019, 0x001D, 0x001E, 0x001F, 0x0020, 0x0022, 0x0023, 0x0024, 0x0029, 0x0062, 0x006B, 0x0072, 0x0074, 0x0084, 0x0085. That's 19 zero-page candidates. Plus more beyond the truncation (we don't see 0x0300+ or 0x0400+). Hmm, truncated at 64 shown of 100.\n\nLet me get the rest by diffing only the ranges 0x0400-0x05FF and 0x0600-0x06FF and 0x0700-0x07FF for w2_pre->w2_post. Wait, w2_pre/w2_post are whole-RAM, so I can diff them with... diff_memory takes two snapshots and considers their full range. Since both are whole-RAM, the diff covers whole RAM. I can't restrict the range in diff_memory. Hmm.\n\nBut I can use `from` chaining with a second hit.\n\nAlternatively, I can snapshot specific ranges with names and diff those, but I don't have range-specific before/after except by taking them now (state changed).\n\nOK, let me just do another controlled hit using slot 3 again (reset to full hearts) and this time narrow via two hits in the SAME spot.\n\nPlan:\n- load slot 3 (full hearts, Link at x100,y150).\n- snapshot A (whole).\n- play up 50 → hit. snapshot B.\n- play down/up again to get hit again? Link overlaps Octorok; maybe repeated hits.\n- snapshot C.\n- diff A->B decreased name=d1; diff B->C decreased name=d2 from d1.\n\nThe problem is getting a second hit reliably.\n\nAlternatively, use the *change* across two hits: health goes full→2.5→... Each hit should produce the same address decreasing. To narrow, I can diff A->C (two hits) with filter decreased AND use `from`? Hmm.\n\nActually simpler: after the first hit (B), health is reduced. Now do another action that reduces health again — walk into the Octorok again. From B (Link at x100,y100 after knockback?), move to collide again.\n\nLet me try: from the current state (2.5 hearts), pla